Maybe I can still do this after all. The implementation covers the essential cart operations: adding items with quantity aggregation, removing items, updating quantities (with auto-removal at zero or below), retrieving individual items or the full list, calculating totals, counting items, clearing the cart, and checking emptiness.

I kept it minimal - no discount systems, no tax calculations, no inventory validation. Just what the tests demand. The map keyed by SKU gives us O(1) lookups, and the error handling follows Go conventions with a sentinel error for missing items.

